# Site secrets (never in the repo)

Real Firebase / site secrets are **never committed** to this repository.

## Canonical location (read here if needed)

`D:\Proyectos\Documents\docs-touraiweb\Secrets\site-config.secrets.js`

Agents may **read** that file when debugging login, auth, or deploy config. Do **not**:

- Commit `js/site-config.secrets.js` or any file with real API keys
- Paste secret values into chat, commits, PRs, or tracked docs
- Add secrets to `site-config.js`, HTML, or locale files

## Local browser testing

The static site loads `js/site-config.secrets.js` (gitignored). If it is missing for local HTTP serving, copy from the canonical path above — that copy stays local and untracked. Production injects the same content via GitHub Actions secret `TOURAI_SITE_CONFIG_SECRETS`.

